# Section spacing

All landing-page sections must share the same layout rhythm.

## Vertical padding

- Use `sectionPaddingYClass` (`py-16 md:py-24`) on every section.
- Do not hand-roll values like `py-12`, `py-20`, or `py-28`.
- The hero uses `Section` with `underFixedHeader` (header clearance + standard bottom padding).
- Sections directly after the hero may use `omitTopPadding` so spacing is not doubled.

## Horizontal gutters

- Section content must use `siteContainerClass` (`container mx-auto px-4 md:px-6 lg:px-8`).
- This matches the navbar in `Header.tsx`. Do not exceed it with wider `px-*`, negative margins, or full-bleed inner wrappers.
- Prefer the `Section` component from `@/components/layout/Section` instead of duplicating classes.

## Example

```tsx
import { Section } from "@/components/layout/Section";

export function Example({ dict }: { dict: SiteDictionary }) {
  return (
    <Section className="bg-gray-50">
      <h2>{dict.example.heading}</h2>
    </Section>
  );
}
```

Tokens live in `@/lib/layout/site-layout.ts`.
